  "section_notes": "S1 imposes rapid reporting and customer notice. S2 sets a 55°C test and a 7% interim failure cap but lacks a permanent 5% limit or sales stop, and keeps per-model results from the general public. S3 requires remote shut-off on new units and a 6-year retrofit with feasibility escape. S4 requires built-in suppression after 36 months. S5 mandates recall at 8/100k with immediate notice but no explicit serious-injury clause."
